================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CODE AND ASSETS
================================================================================

Plumix ships third-party material that keeps its own license. It reaches you
in three forms, handled three ways:

  1. Source copied into this repository. Listed below, because no tool can
     detect copied source — it is recorded by hand and reviewed like any
     other change.

  2. Libraries bundled into the published `@plumix/admin` package. That
     package is the only one published as a bundle, so notices must travel
     with the artifact rather than with an installed dependency. They are
     generated at build time into `dist/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt` inside that
     package, not duplicated here, because the set is large and tracks the
     dependency graph.

  3. Fonts shipped with that same package, as `dist/LICENSE-geist.txt` and
     `dist/LICENSE-geist-mono.txt`.

Every entry is permissively licensed. The admin build fails on any bundled
dependency that is not, so this stays true without anyone having to check.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
shadcn/ui — packages/admin-ui/src
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2023 shadcn
MIT License — https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui

Most components under `packages/admin-ui/src` come from shadcn/ui, kept close
to upstream so `shadcn diff` keeps applying changes. One notice covers the
directory rather than per-file headers, which would break that workflow.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Astro — packages/blocks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2021 Fred K. Schott
MIT License — https://github.com/withastro/astro

The island runtime is derived from Astro's:

  src/serialize.ts                    port of Astro's prop serializer; the
                                      PROP_TYPE codes and payload shape match
                                      byte-for-byte so the SSR/client wire
                                      format stays compatible
  src/island-element.ts               port of `astro-island.ts`
  src/static-html.tsx                 port of `StaticHtml`
  src/island-strategies/visible.ts    adapted from `client:visible`

Plumix diverges from all four; the files describe where and why.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prior art
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Comments across the codebase name projects that informed a design without
contributing code — WordPress, Nuxt, emdash, Puck, Builder.io, and others.
Copyright covers expression, not ideas, so those references carry no license
obligation and none is claimed here. They are engineering context, and the
WordPress ones in particular must never be read as code derivation: WordPress
is GPL, and recording it as such would invent a copyleft obligation that does
not exist.


The MIT License text reproduced at the top of this file applies to each
MIT-licensed entry above.
